Z||000000||Spyro86SE||10-31-2000||12:47 AM||||i was wondering.how hard is it to change a oil pump.and is there any special tools needed.any info would be useful.<P>thanks <BR>"mikey"||||reg||1
Z||000001||TheFiero64||10-31-2000||05:16 PM||||Not hard at all. You must remove the starter, and frount motor mount. ok, you do need to lift the engine a couple of inches with a hoist to get themotor mount to clear. We just did one last week on MattsFiero's car.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/TheFiero64_signature1.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||TheFiero64||10-31-2000||05:18 PM||||almost forgot, I would recommend a Hi-volume pump instead of the stock replacement. A little more money but I think of it as insurance.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/TheFiero64_signature1.gif"> ||||reg||1
